      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's very reassuring, but I'm having a hard time reconciling what you're saying with what's actually on my screen. \n\nHow can a \"High Probability of Capital Erosion\" be considered a \"normal market fluctuation\"? To me, \"capital erosion\" sounds like a very specific and serious threat to my principal, not just some standard volatility. \n\nCan you explain the logic here? Why is the system using such alarming language if my holdings are truly within expected parameters?",
